important when you re doing Set<Integers> or address ranges and you want a quick test to see if a number is present or not.
its ok for the test to give a false positive but not a false negative.

generally the idea is before adding a number to divide and modulo it with a KONSTANT and set the bitpos in the DIV and MODULO 
mask variables.

when asked to test AND with both the masks above if you get the same number back its possibly present else its surely not
present. 

For 32bit numbers use two 64 bit dwords (SSE ANDPS will operate on 128bits at a time so we re good here). Divide and modulo
by 64MB


--------------------
btw you ll also need to setup counters else you ll never be able to reset a bit
